===============================================================================
4. MIXED AND THIRD-PARTY MATERIAL
===============================================================================

The following files are NOT covered by the Robonine copyright above. They are
derived from the upstream SO-ARM100/SO-ARM101 project by TheRobotStudio and are
redistributed under Apache-2.0. See NOTICE.

    simulation/so_arm_101_description/meshes/visual/    base_link.stl,
                                                        link1_1.stl, link2_1.stl,
                                                        link3_1.stl, link4_1.stl
    simulation/so_arm_101_description/meshes/collision/ (convex hulls of the above,
                                                        generated by
                                                        scripts/generate_collision_meshes.py)

link5_1.stl (in both visual/ and collision/) is a single mesh that fuses upstream
SO-ARM101 wrist geometry with Robonine's RB9.01.062.010 Main frame. Until it is
re-exported as two separate meshes, the whole file is distributed under
Apache-2.0: Robonine cannot grant CERN-OHL-P-2.0 over geometry it does not own,
and is free to license its own portion under Apache-2.0.

community/histology-slide-gripper/mujoco/meshes/arm/*.stl are byte-identical
copies of simulation/so_arm_101_description/meshes/visual/*.stl and inherit
their licensing from there.

community/histology-slide-gripper/ was contributed by Michael Viacheslavov
(@histochemichael) and is licensed under the same three-way split; copyright is
held by its author.
